# L34194 — Functional upper blepharoplasty and blepharoptosis repair
library "Blepharoplasty And Blepharoptosis Repair".

// Noridian LCD L34194, version 27, revision R7, effective 2025-10-16.
// A light example: one procedure and eye per assessment, with clinical findings
// and photographic evidence supplied by the reviewer. Source sections A and B
// govern the procedure-specific criteria; cosmetic and minimum-combination rules
// apply to the individual procedure under review.

terminology "Procedure Options":
- system is `http://example.org/crl/CodeSystem/l34194-answer-codes`.
- code is `upper-blepharoplasty` display is `Upper blepharoplasty`.
- code is `blepharoptosis-repair` display is `Blepharoptosis repair`.

terminology "Upper Blepharoplasty Option":
- system is `http://example.org/crl/CodeSystem/l34194-answer-codes`.
- code is `upper-blepharoplasty` display is `Upper blepharoplasty`.

terminology "Functional Complaint Options":
- system is `http://example.org/crl/CodeSystem/l34194-answer-codes`.
- code is `reading` display is `Visual interference affecting reading`.
- code is `driving` display is `Visual interference affecting driving`.
- code is `other-daily-activity` display is `Another daily activity affected by the eyelid-related visual deficit`.
- code is `none` display is `No documented functional deficit affecting daily activities`.

terminology "Upper Eyelid Skin Finding Options":
- system is `http://example.org/crl/CodeSystem/l34194-answer-codes`.
- code is `pseudo-mrd-at-most-2-mm` display is `Overhanging skin causes pseudo-MRD of 2.0 mm or less`.
- code is `medial-lateral-obstruction` display is `Medial or lateral redundant tissue obscures the corresponding line of sight`.
- code is `neither` display is `Neither qualifying skin finding is present`.

concept "Procedure Under Review":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `procedure-under-review`.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- value domain is answer options.
- value from is "Procedure Options".

concept "Cosmetic Surgical Purpose":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `solely-cosmetic-without-functional-benefit`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Documented Patient Complaint":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `functional-complaint-affecting-daily-activities`.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- value domain is answer options.
- value from is "Functional Complaint Options":
  - not qualifying is `none`.

concept "Individual Procedure Necessity Documented":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `individual-procedure-necessity-documented`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Upper Eyelid Skin Finding":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `upper-eyelid-skin-finding`.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- value domain is answer options.
- value from is "Upper Eyelid Skin Finding Options":
  - not qualifying is `neither`.

concept "Ptosis Margin Requirement Met":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `true-mrd-at-most-2-mm-with-relaxed-brows`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Upper Blepharoplasty Photographs Documented":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `upper-blepharoplasty-photographs-documented`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Ptosis Photographs Documented":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `ptosis-photographs-documented`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Upper Blepharoplasty Under Review":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- definition is "Procedure Under Review" in "Upper Blepharoplasty Option".

concept "Qualifying Patient Complaint Reported":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- definition is "Documented Patient Complaint" in qualifying.

concept "Qualifying Skin Finding Documented":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- definition is "Upper Eyelid Skin Finding" in qualifying.

criterion "Functional Necessity Documented":
- when ( "Qualifying Patient Complaint Reported" and "Individual Procedure Necessity Documented" ).

criterion "Upper Blepharoplasty Evidence":
- when ( "Qualifying Skin Finding Documented" and "Upper Blepharoplasty Photographs Documented" ).

criterion "Blepharoptosis Repair Evidence":
- when ( "Ptosis Margin Requirement Met" and "Ptosis Photographs Documented" ).

decision "Blepharoplasty And Blepharoptosis Repair Coverage Determination":
first:
- when "Cosmetic Surgical Purpose" then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
- when "Functional Necessity Documented" then:
    first:
    - when "Upper Blepharoplasty Under Review" then:
        first:
        - when "Upper Blepharoplasty Evidence" then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."certify.Met".
        - otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
        end.
    - otherwise then:
        first:
        - when "Blepharoptosis Repair Evidence" then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."certify.Met".
        - otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
        end.
    end.
- otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".

presentation for "Procedure Under Review":
- question text is "Which procedure is being assessed?".
- question description is "Assess one procedure and eye at a time. For a session with more than one procedure, assess each separately. This example covers functional upper blepharoplasty and blepharoptosis repair.".

presentation for "Cosmetic Surgical Purpose":
- question text is "Is this procedure solely cosmetic, with no functional benefit?".
- question description is "Answer for the procedure being assessed. Functional surgery can also improve appearance; that alone does not make it solely cosmetic.".

presentation for "Documented Patient Complaint":
- question text is "Which daily activity is affected by the eyelid-related visual deficit?".
- question description is "Select the documented functional deficit caused by the eyelid abnormality. Reading and driving are examples; other daily activities can also qualify. The physical signs must be consistent with the complaint in the eye under review.".

presentation for "Individual Procedure Necessity Documented":
- question text is "Is this procedure independently necessary and documented?".
- question description is "Confirm documented necessity for this procedure and eye. If other procedures are planned, this procedure must be part of the minimum combination needed for satisfactory correction; another planned procedure alone must not already achieve the required correction.".

presentation for "Upper Eyelid Skin Finding":
- question text is "Which skin finding is documented for upper blepharoplasty?".
- question description is "Assess the affected eye. Pseudo-MRD measures from the corneal light reflex to the overhanging skin margin, not the actual eyelid margin. Side-gaze obstruction must be caused by predominantly medial or lateral redundant tissue.".

presentation for "Ptosis Margin Requirement Met":
- question text is "Is the actual upper lid MRD 2.0 mm or less, with brows relaxed?".
- question description is "Use the actual eyelid margin in the eye under review, not the overhanging skin margin. MRD is the distance from the corneal light reflex to that margin. This example uses the ordinary resting measurement.".

presentation for "Upper Blepharoplasty Photographs Documented":
- question text is "Do the photographs document the qualifying skin finding?".
- question description is "Photographs must show the same eye and finding recorded above, with sufficient size and detail, patient name and date, and no distorting head or camera tilt. Include frontal and lateral views; oblique views are needed only when the finding is not adequately shown otherwise. Use primary gaze unless another gaze is required to demonstrate the deficit.".

presentation for "Ptosis Photographs Documented":
- question text is "Do the photographs document the qualifying lid position?".
- question description is "Frontal photographs of both eyelids must support the actual-margin MRD for the eye under review, with sufficient quality and detail, patient name and date, and no distorting tilt. A lid obstructing the pupil is a clear-cut finding. Photographic measurement assumes an approximately 11 mm corneal diameter. If the corneal diameter deviates by more than 0.5 mm, document that deviation or include a millimeter ruler approximately in the corneal plane. An ordinary corneal diameter needs neither deviation documentation nor a ruler.".
